Resolutions
23. Consideration of the ratification of a resolution declaring a state of
emergency due to March 1, 2024 fire.
24 - 112
Resolution, Declaring State of Emergency Due to
March 1, 2024 Fire
Attachments:
Jeanine West, EMA, explained the resolution's purpose. West said it would facilitate
any mitigation funding from FEMA.
West acknowledged the cooperation from various county departments, fire districts
and the state in assisting with the fire.
The board thanked staff, the fire districts, and volunteers for their assistance. Acting
Chairman Malm spoke about how special district property taxes assist residents in
their time of need to save homes and lives.
A motion was made by Commissioner Holmes, seconded by
Commissioner Heath, that this agenda item be approved. The motion
carried by the following vote:
Malm, Heath, Holmes, Thompson
Aye:
Lovett
Excused:
